# Harmonized Trio's cost taps "two untapped creatures you control" besides itself (CR 118.3, 602.2b): it cannot be one of the two,
# since the {T} already taps it. With one other creature, or with two of which one is tapped, the ability cannot be activated.
# Turn 3: only one Ornithopter (the other not yet cast) - refused; Bot1 casts the second and attacks with it, which taps it
# (no vigilance), so only one untapped creature besides the Trio is left after that - refused again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Harmonized Trio
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harmonized Trio.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Harmonized Trio.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#1 > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = true
! Bot1.Battlefield.Harmonized Trio.Activate

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Harmonized Trio.Prepared = (absent)
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Harmonized Trio.Tapped = false
